.TH DEVWIDGETS 1 "November 2026" "DevWidgets 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devwidgets \- system and project monitor for developers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devwidgets
[\fB\-\-dark\fR | \fB\-\-light\fR] [\fB\-\-hidden\fR]
[\fB\-\-preferences\fR[=\fIalerts\fR|\fIservers\fR|\fIproject\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows CPU, memory, disk, network, processes, Git, GitHub, Docker,
listening ports and SSH servers in a GTK 4 window, with desktop
alerts and a tray icon where the panel supports StatusNotifierItem;
its right-click menu shows or hides the window, opens Preferences
or quits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-dark, \-\-light
Force a colour scheme instead of following the desktop.
.TP
.B \-\-hidden
Start with the window hidden (only useful with a tray icon).
.TP
.B \-\-preferences
Open the preferences at start, optionally on a page.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Token for the GitHub API; without it the gh command is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/devwidgets/settings.json
Alert limits, servers and the project folder.
